Relevant columns and potential usage  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS  
  – "publication_number": join‑key for everything.  
  – "assignee_harmonized": Variant array with the standardized assignee names → find “DENSO CORP” patents & citing‑side assignees.  
  – "citation": Variant array that lists every cited publication → use it to know which patents are cited.  
  – "cpc": Variant array that lists CPC codes for a publication → take the first element (= “primary” CPC) of the citing patent.  
  – "filing_date": keep only observations whose value > 0 (valid filing date).  

• PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION  
  – "symbol": CPC code (exact string such as ‘H01L21/35’) – join to the first CPC code coming from the citing patent.  
  – "titleFull": Full title of the CPC entry – return as requested “title of the primary CPC subclass”.  

Typical conditions  
• For DENSO patents:  
     WHERE ah.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'  
• Exclude DENSO as citing assignee:  
     AND ca.value::STRING NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'  
• Require valid filing date on both sides:  
     AND t."filing_date" > 0  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex Snowflake SQL snippets (all limited to 20 rows) that build the logic step‑by‑step, ending with a full query that solves the task.  
(Replace LIMIT 20 with any number, remove limits, or wrap into CREATE TABLE / VIEW as needed.)

```sql
-- 1. Inspect the structure of "assignee_harmonized" to see how names are stored.
SELECT t."publication_number",
       ah.value AS "assignee_element"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ah
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quick list of patents that have “DENSO CORP” as (one) assignee.
SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ah
WHERE ah.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
  AND t."filing_date" > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Explore the structure of a "citation" record.
SELECT t."publication_number" AS "citing_pub",
       c.value AS "citation_element"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Extract cited publication numbers from the citation list of a few patents.
SELECT t."publication_number"  AS "citing_pub",
       c.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
WHERE c.value:"publication_number" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Build a quick mapping of {citing → cited} restricted to patents citing any DENSO patent.
WITH denso AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ah
    WHERE ah.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%' )
SELECT t."publication_number"  AS "citing_pub",
       c.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
WHERE c.value:"publication_number"::STRING IN (SELECT * FROM denso)
  AND t."filing_date" > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Attach the assignee(s) of the citing patents while excluding DENSO as citer.
WITH denso AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ah
    WHERE ah.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%' )
SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"            AS "citing_pub",
       ca.value::STRING                           AS "citing_assignee"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ca
WHERE c.value:"publication_number"::STRING IN (SELECT * FROM denso)
  AND t."filing_date" > 0
  AND ca.value::STRING NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Preview the "cpc" array and pick the first (primary) CPC code.
SELECT t."publication_number",
       cp.value:"code"::STRING AS "primary_cpc_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."cpc", OUTER => TRUE) cp
QUALIFY cp.seq = 0              -- first element only
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Join the primary CPC code to its full title in CPC_DEFINITION.
WITH sample AS (
     SELECT t."publication_number",
            cp.value:"code"::STRING AS "primary_cpc_code"
     FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
          LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."cpc", OUTER => TRUE) cp
     QUALIFY cp.seq = 0 )
SELECT s."publication_number",
       s."primary_cpc_code",
       d."titleFull"
FROM sample s
LEFT JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION d
       ON d."symbol" = s."primary_cpc_code"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Put everything together for one random citing patent to verify all pieces.
WITH denso AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ah
    WHERE ah.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%' ),
citing AS (
    SELECT t."publication_number"                              AS "citing_pub",
           ca.value::STRING                                     AS "citing_assignee",
           cp.value:"code"::STRING                              AS "primary_cpc",
           c.value:"publication_number"::STRING                 AS "cited_pub"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ca,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."cpc", OUTER => TRUE) cp
    QUALIFY cp.seq = 0 )
SELECT i.*
FROM citing i
WHERE i."cited_pub" IN (SELECT * FROM denso)
  AND i."citing_assignee" NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL: count citations by (citing assignee × primary CPC subclass title).
WITH denso AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ah
    WHERE ah.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
      AND t."filing_date" > 0 ),

citing_side AS (
    SELECT  t."publication_number"                              AS "citing_pub",
            ca.value::STRING                                    AS "citing_assignee",
            cp.value:"code"::STRING                             AS "primary_cpc",
            c.value:"publication_number"::STRING                AS "cited_pub"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") ca,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."cpc", OUTER => TRUE) cp
    QUALIFY cp.seq = 0  -- first CPC element only
),

joined AS (
    SELECT cs."citing_assignee",
           cs."primary_cpc"
    FROM   citing_side cs
    WHERE  cs."cited_pub" IN (SELECT * FROM denso)
      AND  cs."citing_assignee" NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%' )

SELECT  j."citing_assignee",
        d."titleFull"                     AS "cpc_subclass_title",
        COUNT(*)                          AS "citation_count"
FROM    joined j
LEFT JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION d
       ON d."symbol" = j."primary_cpc"
GROUP BY j."citing_assignee", d."titleFull"
ORDER BY "citation_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
-- Description:
-- Finds all patents assigned to DENSO CORP,
-- detects every external patent that cites one of them,
-- keeps the first CPC code of each citing patent,
-- joins to CPC_DEFINITION for the full subclass title,
-- excludes DENSO CORP itself on the citing side,
-- and returns the citation count per (assignee × CPC title).
```

